R is complaining because you handed the 'oneway' function a single
string parameter.

Instead of 
  oneway = robjects.r['oneway.test']
  test = oneway("values ~ ind, data=d, var.equal=TRUE")
try this:
  test = robjects.r['oneway.test(values ~ ind, data=d, var.equal=TRUE)']
or
  oneway = robjects.r['oneway.test']
  test = oneway("values ~ ind", data=d, var.equal=True)

-Greg

